## The Validation Tier Architecture

The insight about GoalTrajectory versus GapType is precise and generalizes into a clean property for ConnectionPropertyDefinition. The question is not just whether a property is required but **what work block its completion belongs to and what it gates**.

GoalTrajectory on a StoryThread link answers a question that must be answered during Macro Architecture work. An empty GoalTrajectory on a thread connection signals that the author has not yet decided how this scene moves the thread. This is a Stage 1 validation gap — the structural record is incomplete.

GapType on a character connection answers a question that belongs to Scene Architecture work. An empty GapType does not signal that Stage 1 is incomplete. It signals that Stage 2 has not been done for this character in this scene. This is a Stage 2 validation gap — the experience design is incomplete.

A third category exists: properties that are informational annotations with no validation consequence. LogicalOrder is an example — it organizes display but its absence does not signal incomplete work at any stage.

